From 02640f99cb6694d28c8b5f65df75144c9683040a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 17:16:40 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] firewall: DoS protection reports whether it is armed, and the
 Dashboard rail marks its own page

Two field reports from the v3.1.8 beta, one evening.

"DoS protection not enabled when toggled on": the Firewall page showed the
SETTING (fw_dos_x) as the state. rc/firewall.c always emits the SECURITY
chain's rules but hooks `-A FORWARD -i <wan> -j SECURITY` only while the
master switch (fw_enable_x) is on and the box is routing - identical to
stock - so a DoS toggle under a switched-off firewall saved fine and armed
nothing, and the walker's H1 row (the chain's own limit rules, which always
exist) stayed green.
  - httpd status JSON gains dos_armed = fw_dos_x && fw_enable_x && sw_mode==1.
  - Reaper_Firewall.asp dims the DoS toggle with the reason while the master
    switch is off (dosGate()); the status strip reads "off - not armed: ..."
    through the new token RFW_321 (25 dictionaries in lockstep, 6991 lines).
  - reaper_fwsim gains H1b: HASTARGET filter/FORWARD/SECURITY when fw_dos_x=1;
    the feature text names the master switch when fw_enable_x=0; dump_keys
    carries fw_enable_x and fw_dos_x.

The Dashboard's own static left rail (Main_ReaperDash.asp does not use the
shell rail) never marked the Dashboard item current: class="on" on its anchor
plus the .nav a.on / ::before rule mirroring reaper_shell.asp.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
